{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/vupgzmpc","slideIndex":0,"position":{"left":1169.33,"top":1440,"width":965.33,"height":121.33},"name":"Method detail Data preparation and patient state","text":"KNIME standardises patient_summary and patient_detail, retaining identifiers, timestamps, units and missing entries. The source preparation covered 109 workbooks and 112,287 parseable CGM rows.","geometry":"rect","style":{"fontSize":29.33,"typeface":"Arial","color":"#425865","alignment":"left"}}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/wvyh8rqx","slideIndex":0,"position":{"left":1169.33,"top":1582.67,"width":965.33,"height":45.33},"name":"Method Predictive modelling and evaluation","text":"Predictive modelling and evaluation","geometry":"rect","style":{"fontSize":32,"typeface":"Arial","color":"#087F83","bold":true,"alignment":"left"}}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/xw7i1w7i","slideIndex":0,"position":{"left":1169.33,"top":1634.67,"width":965.33,"height":121.33},"name":"Method detail Predictive modelling and evaluation","text":"Train a GRU on 24 historical steps (6 h) to predict the next 15-minute reading. Evaluate against persistence. Investigate a separate conditional model for 12 h trajectories.","geometry":"rect","style":{"fontSize":29.33,"typeface":"Arial","color":"#425865","alignment":"left"}}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/m5wz2h8v","slideIndex":0,"position":{"left":1169.33,"top":1777.33,"width":965.33,"height":45.33},"name":"Method Clinical context and explainability","text":"Clinical context and explainability","geometry":"rect","style":{"fontSize":32,"typeface":"Arial","color":"#087F83","bold":true,"alignment":"left"}}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/n65gvmp0","slideIndex":0,"position":{"left":1169.33,"top":1829.33,"width":965.33,"height":121.33},"name":"Method detail Clinical context and explainability","text":"Neo4j stores medical concepts and source-linked relationships with review status. SHAP feature explanations and risk-based personalised insights remain planned objectives, beyond the Sprint 1 prototypes.","geometry":"rect","style":{"fontSize":29.33,"typeface":"Arial","color":"#425865","alignment":"left"}}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/8reh4rql","slideIndex":0,"position":{"left":1169.33,"top":1972,"width":965.33,"height":45.33},"name":"Method Application integration and verification","text":"Application integration and verification","geometry":"rect","style":{"fontSize":32,"typeface":"Arial","color":"#087F83","bold":true,"alignment":"left"}}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/9s7yxw76","slideIndex":0,"position":{"left":1169.33,"top":2024,"width":965.33,"height":121.33},"name":"Method detail Application integration and verification","text":"React/TypeScript, Flask and Supabase integrate patient records, monitoring, forecasting and graph views. Test role/assignment access and separate measured, predicted and simulated outputs.","geometry":"rect","style":{"fontSize":28,"typeface":"Arial","color":"#425865","alignment":"left"}}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/610ze18z","slideIndex":0,"position":{"left":1169.33,"top":2173.33,"width":965.33,"height":136},"name":"Method scope note","text":"Core twin: data-driven health-state tracking. A 3D body view is a secondary enhancement; autonomous diagnosis and prescription generation are outside scope.","geometry":"rect","style":{"fontSize":29.33,"typeface":"Arial","color":"#7545AB","alignment":"left"}}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/729076pk","slideIndex":0,"position":{"left":1169.33,"top":2486.67,"width":965.33,"height":240},"name":"Conclusions text","text":"Sprint 1 established the data and application foundations for the planned patient-centric twin. GRU forecasting improved on persistence in the reported tests, and a traceable knowledge-graph prototype was integrated. These are research-stage results: the complete risk/XAI/insight workflow, unseen-patient forecasting and reliable intervention simulation remain to be completed or validated.","geometry":"rect","style":{"fontSize":30.67,"typeface":"Arial","color":"#425865","alignment":"left"}}
